Yeast Dataset Classification Analysis
A machine learning project that performs multi-class classification on the yeast protein localization dataset using Random Forest algorithm with comprehensive data analysis and visualization.
Overview
This project analyzes the yeast protein dataset from Kaggle to predict protein localization sites based on various cellular features. It implements a complete machine learning pipeline including data preprocessing, model training, evaluation, and visualization.
Features

Data Loading & Exploration: Automated dataset loading from Kaggle with initial exploratory analysis
Data Preprocessing:

Label encoding for multi-class targets
Feature scaling using StandardScaler
Stratified train-test split for balanced class representation


Model Training: Random Forest Classifier with 100 estimators
Model Evaluation:

Accuracy scoring
Detailed classification reports
5-fold cross-validation
Confusion matrix analysis


Visualizations (6-panel comprehensive analysis):

Feature importance ranking
Confusion matrix heatmap
Class distribution bar chart
PCA visualization (2D projection)
Feature correlation heatmap
Performance metrics comparison

Requirements
kagglehub
pandas
